    {
      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0019",
      "source_en": "Lesson 6. Dots and Ties\n\nA tie combines the durations of two or more notes. Ties and stems are always placed on opposite sides of the notehead. (Rests cannot be tied.)\n\nPractice\n\n1. Practice writing dotted notes in the measures provided.\n\n2. Add one note value to complete each measure.\n\n3. Notate the following rhythm using dotted note values instead of ties. Do not change the duration or beat on which any note begins.\n\n4. Practice tying notes that are on the same line or space.",
